## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical, multilingual, on-device NLP component with concrete constraints and a simple evaluation path.

## Key Concepts
- Lightweight NER: lexicon + rules, tiny ML fallback
- Multilingual tokenization: EN/ES/DE handling
- Taxonomy normalization and confidence scoring
- On-device privacy and rollout strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
function extractMentions(text, lexicon) {
  const mentions = [];
  for (const [word, label] of Object.entries(lexicon)) {
    if (text.includes(word)) mentions.push({ word, label });
  }
  return mentions;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle ambiguous mentions across languages?
- What metrics and thresholds would you use for the confidence score, and how would you validate them on-device?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical multilingual quality checks that balance latency, privacy, and real-world data issues. It also probes how candidates combine simple heuristics with a small model and how they plan evaluation and rollout.

## Key Concepts
- Multilingual NLP basics and translation quality signals
- Hybrid rule-based plus lightweight ML approaches
- Privacy-preserving inference and latency budgeting
- Offline annotation plans and staged canary rollout

## Code Example
```javascript
function simpleMistranslationFlag(src, trans){
  // naive cue: detect presence/absence of 'not' showing sentiment flip
  const sSrc = /not|n't/.test(src) ? -1 : 1;
  const sTrans = /not|n't/.test(trans) ? -1 : 1;
  return Math.abs(sSrc - sTrans) > 0;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale to 10+ languages with minimal drift?
- What metrics and alarms would you attach to the canary rollout?

## Why This Is Asked
Addresses real-time multilingual safety, reduces model hallucinations, and tight latency with on-device processing and privacy-preserving checks.

## Key Concepts
- Retrieval-Augmented Generation
- On-device inference
- External verifier for factuality
- Drift detection and explainability
- Auditable rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-pipeline wiring
const stream = createLiveStream(source);
stream.map(msg => translateToEN(msg)).then(en => {
  const intent = classifyIntent(en);
  const knowledge = fetchKB(en, intent);
  const reply = generatePolicyResponse(knowledge, en);
  if (verifyWithSources(reply, knowledge)) emit(reply);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you keep the private KB synchronized with policy updates without downtime?
- How would you quantify and meet the <180 ms latency target under load?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end design for high-stakes, multilingual NLP with strict latency, privacy, and governance constraints. Probes integration of retrieval-augmented detection, on-device preprocessing, drift-aware evaluation, explainability, and safe rollout strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time streaming NLP
- Retrieval-augmented detection
- On-device PII redaction
- Multilingual DistilBERT variants
- Drift detection and governance
- Explainability and audit logging

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode for pipeline steps
async function infer(text, lang) {
  const redacted = redactPII(text, lang)
  const ctx = encode(redacted, lang)
  const evidence = retriever.search(redacted, lang)
  const score = detector.score(ctx, evidence)
  return { score, evidence }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure and bound the false positive rate across languages?
- How would you implement the rollback and audit logging in production?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical, on-device NLP that yields actionable summaries from multilingual consumer reviews, a realistic Instacart/Amazon use case, without network dependency.

## Key Concepts
- On-device multilang NLP under tight size constraints
- Feature extraction via lightweight POS or rules
- Sentiment aggregation and justification
- Privacy-first data labeling and offline evaluation

## Code Example
```javascript
function scoreFeature(feature, sentences) {
  let score = 0;
  for (const s of sentences) {
    if (s.toLowerCase().includes(feature)) {
      if (/\b(good|great|excellent|loved)\b/.test(s)) score += 1;
      if (/\b(bad|worst|terrible|hate)\b/.test(s)) score -= 1;
    }
  }
  return score;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle negation and language switch within a single sentence?
- How would you validate usefulness of summaries to buyers?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design real-time, privacy-preserving, multilingual NLP pipelines with regulatory constraints and governance.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time streaming architectures (Kafka, Kinesis)
- Privacy-preserving embeddings and federated updates
- NER + relation extraction for ADE
- Per-language drift detection and auditability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo drift detector snippet
function klDivergence(p, q) {
  let sum=0;
  for (let i=0;i<p.length;i++){
    if (p[i]===0||q[i]===0) continue;
    sum += p[i]*Math.log(p[i]/q[i]);
  }
  return sum;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle multilingual tokenization for languages with scarce resources?
- What testing strategy ensures regulatory audit trails are verifiable?
